{
  "about": "Loop-carried flow variables: the shared case list of the orchestration service's FlowVariableMerger and LoopCarriedVariables (continuum-platform-core) and the workbench's FlowVariables.ts. The workbench copies this file verbatim; change the Kotlin rule, the TypeScript rule and this file together.",
  "format": {
    "nodes": "id; loop: true for a loop box; parent: the loop the node is directly inside; inputs: declared input port ids in order (absent = none). Every node has one output port 'out'.",
    "edges": "source.out -> target.targetHandle",
    "steps": "One snapshot each. carried: loop id -> variables carried into this iteration (empty before the first). own: node id -> the variables the node itself set in this snapshot (a missing node set none). expectInherited: node id -> the variables it receives. expectCarriedAfter: loop id -> its carried set after this iteration. expectConditionVariablesBefore: loop id -> what its condition reads with 'carried' as given. expectConditionVariablesAfter: loop id -> what its condition reads at the end of its iteration, that is with only that loop's carried set replaced by its expectCarriedAfter (an enclosing loop's carried set changes only when the enclosing loop's own iteration ends)."
  },
